dig.tik — Display Type Reference
===================================

DESIGN SYSTEM (Gluon-Inspired Dark Theme)
==========================================

Tenets:
  - Dark-first design; near-black backgrounds with subtle layering
  - Minimal, flat UI with depth conveyed through border + shadow, not gradients
  - Content-dense tables as primary data display; no unnecessary decoration
  - Single accent color (blue) for all interactive elements
  - Typography drives hierarchy: weight, size, letter-spacing — not color variety
  - Sticky frosted-glass nav; backdrop-filter blur for depth perception
  - Responsive: collapses nav links on mobile, stacks grids to single column
  - Sections separated by 1px border-top, not gaps or color changes
  - Hero section: centered text, uppercase tag, large bold h1, muted description

Colors:
  --bg-dark:        #0a0a0f       (page background, near-black with blue tint)
  --bg-section:     #111118       (section/dialog backgrounds, slightly lifted)
  --bg-card:        #1a1a24       (card/thead/code backgrounds, 3rd depth level)
  --bg-white:       #ffffff       (light variant sections, inputs)
  --text-primary:   #ffffff       (headings, table data, active links)
  --text-secondary: #a1a1aa       (body text, descriptions, inactive nav)
  --text-muted:     #71717a       (footer links, meta info, placeholders)
  --text-dark:      #18181b       (text on white backgrounds)
  --accent:         #3b82f6       (buttons, active tabs, hover highlights)
  --accent-hover:   #2563eb       (button hover/press state, darker blue)
  --accent-light:   #60a5fa       (tags, session labels, tab active text)
  --border:         #27272a       (all dark borders: sections, tables, cards)
  --border-light:   #e4e4e7       (borders on white/light variant sections)

Typography:
  --font:           system stack (-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI, Roboto)
  --font-mono:      JetBrains Mono, Fira Code, monospace
  Body:             1em/1.6 line-height, antialiased
  h1:               clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.75rem), weight 800, tracking -0.03em
  h2:               1.75rem, weight 700, tracking -0.02em
  h3:               1.25rem, weight 600
  Nav brand:        1.125rem, weight 700, tracking -0.02em
  Table header:     0.75rem, uppercase, weight 600, tracking 0.05em
  Table data:       0.875rem
  Buttons:          0.875–0.9rem, weight 600

Layout:
  Max-width:        1200px (content container)
  Nav height:       64px, sticky, frosted glass (rgba(10,10,15,0.92) + blur(12px))
  Section padding:  5rem vertical, 2rem horizontal
  Hero padding:     6rem vertical
  Border-radius:    8px (standard), 12px (large cards/dialogs)
  Table row hover:  rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.04) — faint blue tint
  Footer:           4-column grid (2fr + 3×1fr), collapses to 1-col on mobile

Orientation:
  - Vertical scroll, single column
  - Nav → Hero → Sections (border-separated) → Footer
  - Content centered within max-width container
  - Tables full-width within container
  - Buttons right-aligned in nav, centered in hero

Preferred Approach: JSP (Server-Side Rendering)
================================================
  *** As of 2026-06-28, all pages use .jsp instead of .xhtml. ***
  *** Database lookups happen server-side via JDBC scriptlets. ***
  *** NO JavaScript fetch() calls for data. DB calls are crisp. ***

  Why:
    - External JS files (js/*.js) were NOT served by the servlet container
    - JavaScript fetch → /api/species returned undefined or failed silently
    - JSP scriptlets execute on the server — data is rendered into HTML before
      the page ever reaches the browser
    - Null values handled at render time: rs.getString("x") != null ? val : ""
    - No "undefined" can ever appear — the HTML is fully formed on delivery

  Pages:
    index.jsp     — Static overview, roadmap, module components table
    species.jsp   — Queries animalia/species tables; drill-down via ?kingdom=&class=&order=&family=
    postal.jsp    — Queries postal table; browse by ?state=
    art.jsp       — Queries art_works table; browse by ?museum=
    science.jsp   — Queries publications table; browse by ?source=
    status.jsp    — Live DB connectivity check, JVM info, servlet container info
    guest.jsp     — Sets 24hr guest cookie, shows client IP, no DB
    register.jsp  — Registration placeholder (points to GitHub Discussions)

  DB Connection (all DB pages):
    Properties dbProps and boolean propsLoaded declared OUTSIDE try block
    (accessible in catch for error diagnostics).
    Loads from WEB-INF/db.properties via application.getResourceAsStream(),
    fallback to getRealPath(), fallback to hardcoded absolute paths.
    Class.forName(dbProps.getProperty("db.driver", "com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver"));
    conn = DriverManager.getConnection(url, user, pass);

  Navigation: Plain <a href="page.jsp?param=value"> links. No AJAX. No dynamic DOM.
  Nav buttons: Guest (text/span on guest.jsp, link elsewhere), Register, Admin →
  Error display: Inline red <p> with e.getMessage() if DB fails.
  CD1 pop-up: Kept on species.jsp only. Minimal inline JS for show/hide toggle.
  welcome-file: index.jsp (configured in WEB-INF/web.xml)

  XHTML equivalents (legacy, client-side JS):
    guest.xhtml    — Client-side IP fetch (api.ipify.org), sets 24hr cookie via JS
    register.xhtml — Registration form, IP detection, cookie-based session

  The .xhtml files remain in the webapp directory for reference but are no longer
  the active deployment. All nav links point to .jsp equivalents.

Interaction:
  - All transitions 0.2s ease (links, buttons, borders)
  - Hover on links: secondary → accent color
  - Hover on table rows: faint blue background
  - Hover on A1 clickable rows: text turns accent blue
  - Buttons: accent → accent-hover on hover
  - Platform badges: lift 2px on hover + border color change
  - Tabs: bottom-border accent blue on active


A1 Type:
=========
  - Standard data table using .table-wrap > <table>
  - Dark header row, bordered cells, compact font
  - Clickable rows expand a hidden child <tr class="a1-child"> beneath them
  - Mouseover of clickable rows highlights text in blue (--accent: #3b82f6)
  - Above each table: white <h3> title + short description <p>
  - Children (expanded rows) use the same table look-and-feel
  - Used across all BMA pages: Species, Postal, Art, Science, Status


CD1 Type (Connector Dialog):
==============================
  *** CAREFUL: css/connector.css does NOT apply on this deployment. ***
  *** All CD1 styles MUST be inline on the HTML elements directly. ***
  *** The external CSS file is not being read/served by the web server. ***

  *** CRITICAL: ALL external JS files (js/*.js) are ALSO NOT served. ***
  *** All JavaScript MUST be inlined into each .xhtml page directly. ***
  *** Do NOT use <script src="js/..."> — it will 404 or return wrong content. ***
  *** The servlet container is not serving static resources from webapp/js/. ***
  *** Symptom: "undefined" displayed in dynamic load elements because the ***
  *** browser cannot load the external .js files, so functions are missing ***
  *** or data values arrive unguarded. ***
  ***                                                                       ***
  *** FIX (2026-06-28): All JS inlined into species.xhtml, status.xhtml,  ***
  *** index.xhtml. Added safeName() guard in species-loader to ensure no   ***
  *** null/undefined value ever reaches textContent or innerHTML.           ***
  *** config.xml fetch guarded against parse errors and missing elements.   ***
  
  - Black button PNG (transparent background) from resources/black.button.png
  - Button centered between hero header and page content
  - All styles inline — wrapper: display:flex;justify-content:center
  - Button: all:unset;display:block;margin:0 auto;background:transparent
  - Image: 80x80px fixed, border-radius:50%, background:transparent
  - JS handles press transition: transform scale(0.9) + blue glow drop-shadow
  - Transition uses cubic-bezier(0.42,-1.84,0.42,1.84) spring easing from resources/button.css
  - Floating dialog: position:fixed;top:50%;left:50%;transform:translate(-50%,-50%)
  - Click button → opens connector dialog. Click again → closes it
  - Click anywhere off the dialog (overlay) → closes it
  - Textarea default placeholder: 'Connection idle...'
  - Double-click textarea → restores any previously saved content
  - Idle 20 minutes: close dialog, clear textarea, keep connection info
  - Idle 60 minutes (total): full circuit reset — clear all memory
  - On close: save textarea content internally, clear visible text
  - Controls: dropdown (Connect/Disconnect/Poll Area Data/Hard Reset), Send, OK
  - Send/OK buttons same blue (#3b82f6)
  - Files: js/connector.js (CSS file exists but is NOT used — inline only)


Reference: lauradei.us/brarner.m.alete/
Created: 2026-06-27
Updated: 2026-06-27 (Design system + CD1 documented)


Script Permissions (chmod +x)
==============================
Run after clone/checkout to make all scripts executable:

  chmod +x build.sh
  chmod +x install/check-db.sh
  chmod +x install/deploy-local.sh
  chmod +x install/deploy-remote-linux.sh
  chmod +x install/download-jars.sh
  chmod +x install/generate-integrity.sh
  chmod +x install/install_ai_jars.sh
  chmod +x install/install_jars.sh
  chmod +x install/install_macos.sh
  chmod +x install/install-mysql-linux.sh
  chmod +x install/install_mysql.sh
  chmod +x install/install.sh
  chmod +x install/populate-all.sh
  chmod +x install/populate-art.sh
  chmod +x install/populate-postal.sh
  chmod +x install/populate-publications.sh
  chmod +x install/populate-science-db.sh
  chmod +x install/populate-ssa.sh
  chmod +x install/run_create_science_db.sh
  chmod +x install/test-jdbc.sh
  chmod +x install/test-local.sh
  chmod +x install/test-remote.sh
  chmod +x install/verify-integrity.sh
  chmod +x install/after-pull.sh
  chmod +x install/macos/deploy-local.sh
  chmod +x install/macos/install-mysql-macos.sh
  chmod +x install/macos/populate-all.sh
  chmod +x install/macos/populate-science-db.sh
  chmod +x install/macos/test-jdbc.sh

One-liner:
  find . -name "*.sh" -exec chmod +x {} \;


Database & Install Work Log (2026-06-28)
=========================================

Session summary of all changes made to get the BMA database and JSP pages
fully operational on both local dev and remote server (Xenu-X900).

1. CREATED DATABASE & TABLES
   - Created `BrarnerScience` database on MySQL (root@localhost / $$Ironman1)
   - Tables: animalia, species, postal, art_works, publications, ssa_offices
   - Final schema fixes:
     * postal: added latitude DECIMAL(9,6), longitude DECIMAL(9,6)
     * art_works: added collection VARCHAR(100)
     * publications: added abstract_text TEXT

2. GENERATED CSV DATA FILES (data/)
   - data/postal/us-zip-codes.csv — 52 NC entries with lat/lon
   - data/species/animalia.csv — 3,008 rows (extracted from source/species/**/config.xml)
   - data/ssa/ssa-offices.csv — 1,182 rows (extracted from source/ssa/**/config.xml)
   - data/art/art-works.csv — 32 rows (11 NC museums)
   - data/publications/publications.csv — 20 rows (8 journals)
   - Fixed apostrophe in COEUR D'ALENE that broke SQL inserts

3. FIXED POPULATE SCRIPTS (install/)
   - populate-postal.sh: DROP+CREATE table with correct schema before insert
   - populate-art.sh: DROP+CREATE with collection column
   - populate-publications.sh: DROP+CREATE with abstract_text column
   - populate-ssa.sh: batched all INSERTs into single SQL file (was spawning
     mysql per row = 1182 "password on command line" warnings)
   - All scripts now: DROP IF EXISTS → CREATE with full schema → batch INSERT
   - Eliminated per-row mysql calls across all populate scripts

4. FIXED populate-science-db.sh TABLE DEFINITIONS
   - postal: added latitude, longitude columns
   - art_works: added collection column
   - publications: added abstract_text column

5. UPDATED db.properties
   - db.user=root
   - db.password=$$Ironman1
   - db.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/BrarnerScience

6. JSP PAGES CONFIRMED WORKING
   - postal.jsp — queries postal table, browse by ?state=
   - art.jsp — queries art_works table, browse by ?museum=
   - science.jsp — queries publications table, browse by ?source=
   - All three render server-side via JDBC, no JS, no "undefined"

7. EMBEDDED TOMCAT LAUNCHER
   - Created: servlets/servlet/src/main/java/com/mearvk/servlet/BmaEmbeddedTomcat.java
   - Compiles against jars/* (tomcat-embed-core, jasper, el, jakarta APIs)
   - Serves at http://localhost:8080/brarner.m.alete/

8. DOWNLOADED JARS (jars/)
   - tomcat-embed-core-11.0.2.jar (3.4M)
   - tomcat-embed-jasper-11.0.2.jar (632K) — provides org.apache.jasper.runtime
   - tomcat-embed-el-11.0.2.jar (262K)
   - jakarta.servlet-api-6.1.0.jar (390K)
   - jakarta.servlet.jsp-api-4.0.0.jar (65K)
   - jakarta.el-api-6.0.1.jar (92K)
   - jakarta.annotation-api-3.0.0.jar (26K)
   - ecj-3.37.0.jar (3.2M) — Eclipse compiler for JSP runtime compilation
   - mysql-connector-j-8.3.0.jar (2.4M)
   - All under 50MB — nothing gitignored

9. CREATED check-db.sh (install/)
   - Queries all tables, prints row counts, shows populated/empty status

10. CREATED PLATFORM SCRIPTS
    install/windows/ (.bat):
      check-db, populate-all, populate-science-db, populate-postal,
      populate-art, populate-publications, populate-ssa, download-jars,
      deploy-local, test-local

    install/macos/ (.sh):
      check-db, populate-all, populate-science-db, populate-postal,
      populate-art, populate-publications, populate-ssa, download-jars,
      deploy-local, test-local

    All scripts chmod +x. One-liner: find . -name "*.sh" -exec chmod +x {} \;

KEY LESSON: ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS does not work reliably across
MySQL versions. Use DROP TABLE IF EXISTS + CREATE TABLE with the full correct
schema instead. This guarantees the populate scripts work on any fresh install.


Updates (2026-06-28, session 2)
================================

11. FIXED dbProps SCOPE BUG (all DB pages)
    - Properties dbProps and boolean propsLoaded were declared inside the try block
    - The catch block referenced them for error diagnostics → "cannot be resolved"
    - Fix: moved declarations above try in species.jsp, postal.jsp, art.jsp,
      science.jsp, status.jsp

12. CREATED guest.jsp + register.jsp
    - guest.jsp: sets bma_guest cookie (24hr), shows client IP via
      request.getHeader("X-Forwarded-For") / request.getRemoteAddr()
      "Guest" rendered as text (span), not a link, on that page
    - register.jsp: placeholder pointing to GitHub Discussions for registration

13. CREATED guest.xhtml (legacy equivalent)
    - Client-side: fetches IP from api.ipify.org, sets bma_session cookie via JS
    - Same nav structure as other .xhtml pages

14. ADDED Guest + Register BUTTONS TO ALL PAGES
    - All 6 main JSP pages (index, species, postal, art, science, status)
      now show: Guest | Register | Admin → in nav-actions

15. DEPLOY/TEST SCRIPTS NOW AUTO-DISCOVER JSP FILES
    - deploy-local.sh, deploy-remote-linux.sh: dynamic find for JSP summary
    - test-local.sh, test-remote.sh, macos/test-local.sh, windows/test-local.bat:
      iterate all *.jsp in webapp dir instead of hardcoded list
    - install.sh: updated hardcoded JSP list to include guest.jsp, register.jsp

16. FIXED test-local.sh GREP PATTERNS
    - Was using grep -qi with \| alternation (requires -E flag)
    - Changed to grep -qiE throughout
    - Updated species.jsp expected pattern to match actual rendered content
      (Amphibia|Mammalia|Animalia|<td>)
    - Result: 15 passed, 0 failed

17. CREATED install/after-pull.sh
    - Syncs webapp source → Tomcat deploy dir via rsync (skips db.properties)
    - Restarts Tomcat only if JARs or web.xml changed
    - Reloads Apache2 only if css/ or images/ changed
    - No-op if nothing changed
    - Usage: sudo bash install/after-pull.sh [tomcat_home]
